4. CLIProxyAPI plugin loader/ABI — internal/pluginabi/,
   internal/pluginhost/, internal/plugintest/ fixture,
   examples/plugin/echo/ (adapted, not verbatim)

   Upstream: github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI, commit
   250d598175db61a4e99ac38b9164ed04745754e5.
   License: MIT (LICENSE at that commit reads "MIT License /
   Copyright (c) 2025-2005.9 Luis Pater / Copyright (c)
   2025.9-present Router-For.ME" — verbatim upstream text).

   Adapted (renamed to the castctl namespace,
   castctl_plugin_init; castctl schema 1 instead of upstream
   schema 10): the C loader preamble and entry-symbol/ABI
   checks (loader_unix.go), the Windows loader table shape
   (loader_windows.go), the no-cgo stub refusal
   (loader_unsupported.go), the host/client/loader interface
   shape (abi.go), ApplyConfig/quiesce/rollback (host.go),
   discovery and candidate dirs (platform.go), the shadow
   copy (shadow.go), the guarded call (client_guard.go),
   the lifecycle envelope shape (rpc_schema.go, rpc_client.go),
   the ABI/schema constants (sdk/pluginabi/types.go), the
   capabilities shape (sdk/pluginapi/types.go), and the
   verify-before-use checksum idea
   (internal/pluginstore/checksum.go). Deliberately NOT
   taken: host.auth.* callbacks, the PluginsConfig
   store/config schema, min_version/allow_downgrade, random
   shadow names/memfd, and load-time signature checks. The
   The Lstat component check (all platforms) and hardlink
   (linux/darwin/freebsd only) shadow hardening and the glibc compat gate
   are castctl-original. Full mapping in docs/provenance.md
   §2 and docs/plugins.md References.

   Nothing else in this tree is copied upstream code. In particular,
   no sing-box, go-telegram/bot, utls, or Noise-spec
   source is copied into the tree.

